  "name": "Push NASA picture of the day and nearest asteroid data to Home Assistant",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "094fb25e-04c0-4672-94c6-eca1ef3ebca0",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -768,
        -208
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 1,
        "width": 640,
        "height": 1160,
        "content": "## Push NASA picture of the day and nearest asteroid data to Home Assistant\n\n### Who's it for\nHome Assistant users who want a daily dose of space on their dashboard: NASA's Astronomy Picture of the Day plus the closest asteroid passing Earth this week.\n\n### How it works\n**When 6AM Daily** (or **Manual Test Trigger**) starts two parallel branches:\n- **APOD:** fetches the Astronomy Picture of the Day from NASA's science.nasa.gov feed (no API key), keeps the title, image (or video thumbnail), date and an explanation trimmed to 280 characters, and upserts `sensor.nasa_apod`.\n- **Asteroid:** fetches NASA's 3-day Near-Earth Object feed, sorts every approach by miss distance, and upserts `sensor.nasa_asteroid` with name, date, distance, size, speed and hazard flag.\n\n### Setup steps\n1. Get a free API key at https://api.nasa.gov.\n2. Create a **Query Auth** credential: name `api_key`, value = your key. Select it in **Fetch Asteroid Feed**. (The APOD feed needs no key; NASA retired the old api.nasa.gov APOD endpoint in October 2026.)\n3. Create a **Home Assistant** credential (base URL + long-lived access token) and select it in both **Send ... to Home Assistant** nodes.\n4. Run **Manual Test Trigger**, then check Developer Tools > States in Home Assistant.\n5. Activate the workflow.\n\n### Requirements\nHome Assistant with API access, a free NASA API key.\n\n### Customization\nChange the schedule, the explanation length in **Set APOD Fields**, the look-ahead window in **Fetch Asteroid Feed**, or the entity IDs. Show the picture with a Picture Entity card using `image_url`.\n\n**Note:** sensors created through the Home Assistant API disappear after a Home Assistant restart until the next run."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "0f9bb136-839e-401c-8a38-c8f82ea759d6",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -48,
        -208
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 240,
        "height": 656,
        "content": "## Workflow start triggers\n\nContains the scheduled 6 AM trigger and the manual test trigger that both launch the APOD and asteroid data branches."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "000405ba-21f9-4b74-987a-f721a54cbdea",
      "name": "Sticky Note2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        224,
        -112
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 640,
        "height": 320,
        "content": "## Fetch and send APOD\n\nTop-row branch that retrieves NASA's Astronomy Picture of the Day, extracts the title, explanation, image URL, and media type, then pushes those values to Home Assistant."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "89b674ee-1dd5-4c42-9687-d30283091af4",
      "name": "Sticky Note3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        224,
        240
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 864,
        "height": 320,
        "content": "## Process asteroid data\n\nLower-row branch that retrieves the NASA near-Earth object feed, prepares the asteroid count and raw objects, runs custom code to find the closest asteroid, and sends the result to Home Assistant."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "9eb42085-8859-42fa-bd81-165c00bd13c9",
      "name": "When 6AM Daily",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "triggerAtHour": 6
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.3
    },
    {
      "id": "d43319d5-4b4e-4d0f-a4d7-9c76ea36888a",
      "name": "Fetch NASA APOD Data",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "maxTries": 3,
      "position": [
        272,
        48
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "url": "https://science.nasa.gov/wp-json/wp/v2/apod-basic",
        "method": "GET",
        "options": {},
        "sendQuery": true,
        "specifyQuery": "keypair",
        "queryParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "per_page",
              "value": "1"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "typeVersion": 4.4,
      "waitBetweenTries": 5000
    },
    {
      "id": "1089476d-fcb7-402f-b9dc-c2cc22aecc70",
      "name": "Set APOD Fields",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "position": [
        496,
        48
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "apod-title",
              "name": "title",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ String($json.title || '').replace(/<[^>]*>/g, '').trim() }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "apod-explanation",
              "name": "explanation",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ (() => { const t = String($json.explanation || '').replace(/<[^>]*>/g, '').replace(/&nbsp;/g, ' ').replace(/^\\s*Explanation:\\s*/i, '').replace(/\\s+/g, ' ').trim(); return t.length > 280 ? t.substring(0, 277) + '...' : t; })() }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "apod-url",
              "name": "image_url",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ $json.media_type === 'image' ? ($json.hdurl || $json.url) : ($json.thumbnail_url || $json.hdurl || $json.url) }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "apod-media-type",
              "name": "media_type",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ $json.media_type }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "apod-date",
              "name": "date",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ $json.date }}"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 3.4
    },
    {
